From: jaylfc <jaylfc25@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: s5kjn1 link freq 700MHz

The s5kjn1 endpoint declares a 600MHz link frequency, but the driver only
supports S5KJN1_LINK_FREQ_700MHZ. With the 19.2MHz MCLK patch applied the
sensor gets past its clock check and then fails here instead:

  s5kjn1 18-002d: no matching link frequencies found
  s5kjn1 18-002d: error -ENOENT: failed to check HW configuration

700000000 is the value upstream uses for this sensor on this board (patch 2/2
of Danila Tikhonov"s ultra-wide series). Only the s5kjn1 endpoint is touched:
the imx471 endpoint also declares 600MHz and its driver accepts it, so
changing that would break a camera that already binds.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -933,8 +933,8 @@
 		port {
 			camera_s5kjn1_ep: endpoint {
 				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
 				bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
-				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
 				remote-endpoint = <&csiphy2_ep>;
 			};
 		};
